  <issue>
  Support casting from `uuid` to object types
We want to support doing things like `<User><uuid>$0` (and probably just `<User>$0`, with the same meaning?), and have it mean something like
`assert_exists((select detached User filter .id = <uuid>$0))`
(probably with a better error message passed to assert_exists).

This will make it a lot easier to convert ids into objects.

Offline we've discussed a bunch of alternative syntaxes and decided that just supporting casting was the least bad. If anyone wants I guess we can argue more here now.
  </issue>
  
